  "chatHistory": [
    {
      "userId": "user-demo-1",
      "role": "user",
      "content": "How do I maintain good squat form?",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-14T17:06:41.293Z"
    },
    {
      "userId": "user-demo-1",
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here is the biomechanical checklist for a flawless **Bodyweight Squat**:\n\n1. **Stance**: Feet shoulder-width apart, toes flared slightly out (10-15 degrees) to allow room for your pelvis.\n2. **First Move**: Initiate by hinging your hips back slightly before bending the knees.\n3. **Depth**: Lower until hip crease is level with knee joint (parallel). Keep your chest proud and eyes forward.\n4. **Knee Alignment**: Keep your knees pushed out in line with your second toe—do not allow them to collapse inward.\n5. **Ascent**: Drive through your entire foot (tripod foot pressure) and squeeze glutes at the top.\n\n💡 *Pro Tip*: Use our **Camera Vision Mode**! It tracks your hip-knee-ankle angles in real time to verify your depth.",
      "provider": "heuristic_fallback",
      "category": "exercise_technique",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-14T17:06:41.302Z"
    },
    {
      "userId": "user-demo-1",
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I feel sharp knee pain when bending down",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-14T17:06:41.323Z"
    },
    {
      "userId": "user-demo-1",
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "⚠️ **Safety First Adventurer!** \n\nIf you are experiencing sharp pain, swelling, dizziness, or joint discomfort, **please stop exercising immediately**. \n\n- **Do NOT push through pain**: Genuine joint or tendon pain is a signal from your nervous system to rest and protect the joint.\n- **R.I.C.E Principle**: Rest, Ice (if acute swelling), Compression, and Elevation.\n- **Non-Medical Disclaimer**: I am an AI fitness coach, not a medical doctor or licensed physical therapist. If pain persists beyond 24-48 hours or radiates, please consult a qualified healthcare professional.\n\nWould you like to switch to a gentle **Parasympathetic Breathing Flow** or take a safe **Active Recovery Rest Day**? Rest days preserve your adventure streak!",
      "provider": "safety_guardrail",
      "category": "safety_advisory",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-14T17:06:41.327Z"
    }
  ]
